 "summary": "Relates to eliminating the electronic death registration system fee for funeral directors and undertakers.",
 "title": "Relates to eliminating the electronic death registration system fee for funeral directors and undertakers; repealer",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A4439",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A4439-2023",
     "printNo": "A4439",
     "session": 2023,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 47\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 4439, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the public health law, in relation to eliminating\n      the electronic death registration system fee for funeral directors\n      and undertakers; and to repeal provisions  of  such  law  relating\n      thereto\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would  repeal current law that establishes a twenty dollar\nfee for each burial or removal permit issued to each funeral director or\nundertaker to support the establishment and maintenance of the Electron-\nic Death Registration  System  (EDRS)  operated  by  the  Department  of\nHealth.  The fee is paid by the funeral directors, who agreed in 2013 to\nfund  the  development  of  the EDRS through this funding mechanism. The\nrevenue stream supports the maintenance  of  the  system  and  necessary\nimprovements.\n \n  This  bill  is  identical  to  legislation I vetoed last year, and any\nchanges to the funding mechanism for the  EDRS  are  more  appropriately\ndiscussed within the context of the State budget.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 47,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2023
   }
  ],
  "size": 1
 },
